### Motions
move max moon menu map method
END_CODE

{
    desc => 'Regex n navigates across empty lines',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Action: /m. then n repeatedly — must skip empty lines correctly

Regression test for GTK forward_to_line_end bug on empty lines.
Bug: line_text() returned next-line content for empty lines,
causing search_forward to find matches beyond the empty line's
actual length. set_cursor clamped the out-of-bounds column to 0,
creating an infinite loop where n kept "finding" the same match.

_1.png (initial state):
- Dark theme, Normal mode, cursor at line 1, col 0
- Multiple empty lines between content

Action: keystrokes "/m.\\nn" (search regex m., press n once)

_2.png (first n):
- First /m. highlights all matches on non-empty lines
- First n moves from "mi" in "Vim" (line 1) to "me" in
  "Documentation" (line 1, col 19)

Action: keystrokes "n" (second n)

_3.png (second n — crosses empty line):
- Second n skips past "me", crosses the empty line (line 2),
  and lands on "me" in "Version" (line 3, col 14)
- This is the critical test: n must NOT get stuck on the
  empty line between "Documentation" and "Version"

Action: keystrokes "nnnnnn" (six more n presses to cycle through all matches)

_4.png (all matches visited):
- Cursor has cycled through all m. matches without getting stuck
- Matches visited: Vim(mi), Documentation(me), Version(me),
  SourceEditor(me), Normal(mo), Motions(mo), move(mo),
  max(ma), moon(mo), menu(me), map(ma), method(me)
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->editor->set_theme('dark');
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('1');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('/m.\n');
        $ctx->delay(300);
        $ctx->snapshot('2');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('n');
        $ctx->delay(200);
        $ctx->snapshot('3');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('nnnnnn');
        $ctx->delay(300);
        $ctx->snapshot('4');
    },
}
